<title>FRANCE: GdE sees 6.0 bln francs profit in 1999.</title>
<headline>GdE sees 6.0 bln francs profit in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Generale des Eaux chairman Jean-Marie Messier said that for 1999 he expected a 12 percent return on equity, or a net profit figure of six billion francs.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking for 1999 an at least 12 percent return on equity, which means basically a six billion French francs net result. Before amortisation of goodwill, the return would be close to 15 percent,&quot; Messier told Reuters Financial Television in an interview.</p>
<p>On Thursday, Generale said it expected a 1997 net profit of at least five billion francs.</p>
</text>
